WEBVTT

00:08.758 --> 00:11.803
[static buzzing]

00:13.555 --> 00:17.684
[upbeat music]

00:40.040 --> 00:42.751
[man 1] Man, thought you'd be
off the clock by five,

00:42.834 --> 00:45.712
they keep you on call. Shitluck.

00:46.296 --> 00:48.047
[man 2] Cap said I could leave
my gun and badge

00:48.131 --> 00:50.049
if I went home to listen to my old lady

00:50.133 --> 00:55.096
go on and on about her online shopping
or whatever the hell she did all day.

00:55.180 --> 00:57.974
[man 1] That’s what you get
for choosing the life of a public servant.

00:58.057 --> 01:00.435
[man 2] It just had to fucking rain.

01:00.518 --> 01:03.104
Hmm? What the hell you doin'? Back it up.

01:03.188 --> 01:04.272
Looking to get shot?

01:04.355 --> 01:05.231
[gasps, shouts]

01:06.983 --> 01:09.652
[music ends]

01:12.363 --> 01:13.656
[man grunts]

01:19.788 --> 01:23.458
[guns firing]

01:27.921 --> 01:29.130
[grunting and groaning]

01:30.882 --> 01:33.176
-[shouts]
-Got us a cyber psycho!

01:33.843 --> 01:35.678
Raise MaxTac now!

01:36.596 --> 01:37.430
[gasps]

01:48.441 --> 01:50.819
[shouting]

01:59.661 --> 02:00.787
[shouts]

02:31.192 --> 02:32.861
We need to fry the system fast.

02:32.944 --> 02:35.113
Freak's supporting military-grade ICE!

02:35.196 --> 02:37.824
Meaning that our tech isn't? Get to it!

02:44.664 --> 02:49.460
[upbeat music]

03:13.484 --> 03:16.362
[shouting]

03:16.446 --> 03:20.825
-[laid-back music]
-[groaning, gasps]

03:20.909 --> 03:22.285
[Ripperdoc] So, what do you think?

03:22.911 --> 03:25.288
Still warm, that. Couple hours old.

03:25.371 --> 03:27.498
Lifted from the edgerunner
who scrolled it.

03:27.582 --> 03:29.250
Straight off the street.

03:29.334 --> 03:30.752
So, what!

03:30.835 --> 03:34.130
Doc, hey, you gotta tell me
who keeps feeding you these nuggets.

03:34.213 --> 03:35.590
Kurosaki. Who else?

03:35.673 --> 03:38.760
Ain't no other editor who churns out
BDs that sweet and preem.

03:38.843 --> 03:41.095
Won't pull nothin' like that
off the shelf, neither.

03:41.179 --> 03:44.265
No shit. Brain's still buzzing.
Gonna be sick.

03:44.349 --> 03:46.351
Slow, deep breaths, choom.

03:46.434 --> 03:49.103
Just left the head
of a skezzed-out chrome junkie.

03:49.187 --> 03:51.105
Cyberpsychosis ain't no joke.

03:51.189 --> 03:54.317
Anyway, either hurt or don't,
got more chips for you to slot.

03:54.400 --> 03:55.777
Really? What?

03:55.860 --> 03:58.029
Something special.

03:58.112 --> 03:59.197
[buzzing]

03:59.280 --> 04:01.783
-[David] Huh? Cut the shit, man!
-[erotic moaning]

04:01.866 --> 04:03.451
[buzzing]

04:03.534 --> 04:07.330
[machine whirring]

04:08.164 --> 04:11.084
[sighs]

04:12.043 --> 04:15.463
-[machine beeping]
-Huh?

04:15.546 --> 04:18.383
[automated voice] Cycle suspended
due to insufficient funds.

04:18.466 --> 04:21.469
-Geez, not again.
-Cycle suspended due to in--

04:21.552 --> 04:23.805
[reporter] It was a tragic scene
in Westbrook today

04:23.888 --> 04:24.973
when a corporate convoy

04:25.056 --> 04:27.850
-was ambushed by 6th Street…
-[sighs] God, Mom.

04:27.934 --> 04:30.186
[both gasp and sigh]

04:30.270 --> 04:31.229
Morning, Miho.

04:31.312 --> 04:33.064
If you keep sleeping on the couch,

04:33.147 --> 04:35.024
gonna get early onset arthritis.

04:35.108 --> 04:37.860
I know. Just dead
after my night shift, is all.

04:37.944 --> 04:41.239
[David] You and the washing machine both.
Forget to re-up it?

04:41.322 --> 04:42.865
[mom stammers] Yeah.

04:42.949 --> 04:44.826
I'll take care of it later, 'kay?

04:44.909 --> 04:48.121
Oh, money, right.
You mentioned a reef update for class.

04:48.204 --> 04:50.081
That happen yet?
When did you say you need it?

04:50.164 --> 04:54.002
No, no. It's fine. Got Doc to handle it.

04:54.836 --> 04:58.131
-What do you mean "handle it"?
-I'm good. All set.

04:58.214 --> 05:00.300
[mom] Don't go cutting corners, D.

05:00.383 --> 05:04.387
Already cashed my paycheck.
You'll get it updated right. Hear me?

05:04.470 --> 05:07.307
Mom, seriously!
Just feed the washer, alright?

05:07.390 --> 05:09.767
[mom] I forgot this time. I told you.

05:10.643 --> 05:12.478
Promise me you'll buy the update.

05:12.562 --> 05:14.397
Okay, okay.

05:14.480 --> 05:17.317
And you're really going to school
dressed like that?

05:17.400 --> 05:18.568
-Uniform’s soaked.
-[sighs]

05:18.651 --> 05:20.069
-[reporter] A military-grade implant…
-[gasps]

05:20.153 --> 05:21.404
-…was found missing from the body
-Hmm?

05:21.487 --> 05:24.407
of Lt. Col. James Norris,
shot dead by MaxTac…

05:24.490 --> 05:27.785
Mom, you're on TV! Nova!

05:27.869 --> 05:30.663
-Not Nova, David. A bloodbath.
-[TV pings off]

05:30.747 --> 05:34.000
-Go on. Off to school.
-[gasps] Bye.

05:34.083 --> 05:35.626
Love you, Miho.

05:36.127 --> 05:39.172
[phone ringing]

05:40.715 --> 05:43.426
Maine? It's Gloria.

05:45.219 --> 05:48.139
["Who's Ready for Tomorrow" playing]

05:50.725 --> 05:54.020
Hmm…

05:58.858 --> 06:00.526
♪ I ain't your average sicko ♪

06:00.610 --> 06:02.278
♪ I'm dead, just like disco ♪

06:02.361 --> 06:05.740
♪ My bank account
Is zero-zero-zero, oh no ♪

06:05.823 --> 06:07.867
♪ I think I need a hero ♪

06:07.950 --> 06:09.452
♪ I don't have no ego ♪

06:09.535 --> 06:11.621
♪ 'Cause I'm spinnin' out now ♪

06:11.704 --> 06:14.373
-[man crying]
-[kid shouting]

06:14.957 --> 06:17.752
[panicked moaning]

06:17.835 --> 06:19.629
[retching]

06:19.712 --> 06:23.132
♪ And now I'm getting older
My heart is growing colder ♪

06:23.216 --> 06:25.968
♪ Oh, that's fine ♪

06:31.015 --> 06:34.268
[automated voice] Trauma Team.
Clear a path immediately.

06:34.852 --> 06:38.106
Emergency evac underway. Emergency evac.

06:38.189 --> 06:40.858
All AVs, vacate the airway.

06:40.942 --> 06:45.279
Trauma Team. Clear a path immediately.
Trauma Team. Clear a path.

06:45.363 --> 06:46.531
Don't walk.

06:48.199 --> 06:49.283
Don't walk.

06:50.952 --> 06:55.039
-Walk. Walk. Walk.
-[rapid beeping]

06:55.123 --> 06:57.542
Walk. Walk.

07:01.379 --> 07:04.674
♪ And now I'm getting older
My heart is growing colder ♪

07:04.757 --> 07:07.677
♪ Oh, that's fine ♪

07:08.469 --> 07:14.183
♪ I was a teenage outlaw
With no worries on my mind ♪

07:15.351 --> 07:18.563
♪ And now I'm getting older
My heart is growing colder ♪

07:18.646 --> 07:20.440
♪ Oh, that's fine ♪

07:22.650 --> 07:24.026
[gasps]

07:28.698 --> 07:32.076
♪ You say it's over ♪

07:32.160 --> 07:35.121
[gasping] Huh?

07:36.080 --> 07:38.249
[sighs, scoffs]

07:41.752 --> 07:43.838
[upbeat music]

07:58.978 --> 07:59.812
[grunts]

08:00.855 --> 08:02.773
Good morning to you, class.

08:02.857 --> 08:05.776
Today's attendance. Zero absences.

08:05.860 --> 08:07.445
Martinez, David.

08:07.528 --> 08:10.114
You are not in compliance
with the Academy's dress code.

08:10.198 --> 08:12.116
Yeah. Real sorry about that.

08:12.200 --> 08:14.285
Afraid my uniform's still
at the cleaner's.

08:14.368 --> 08:16.329
-[grunts]
-[lecturer] Do you have a spare uniform?

08:16.412 --> 08:17.872
Yeah. Spare's there too.

08:17.955 --> 08:21.959
[lecturer] Understood. Please submit
a Uniform Exception form after class.

08:22.043 --> 08:24.295
-[hiss]
-Now, let us begin today's lesson.

08:24.378 --> 08:27.840
-You will observe…
-[Katsuo] Gutter rat. Rat off the street.

08:27.924 --> 08:30.426
Me? Nah. Wouldn't show my face.

08:30.510 --> 08:34.096
[David] Cray-crazy, I know,
but some of us here to learn to learn.

08:34.180 --> 08:35.973
[Katsuo] With that fossiltech?

08:36.057 --> 08:38.559
Updates, man. Bet it's not compatible.

08:38.643 --> 08:40.561
[David] I made it compatible.

08:40.645 --> 08:42.480
[Katsuo] Huh? How?

08:42.563 --> 08:44.065
[David] How I had to.

08:44.148 --> 08:45.775
[Katsuo] Life's gotta be gotta be shit

08:45.858 --> 08:48.319
when a two-bit wreath
costs your life savings.

08:48.402 --> 08:49.237
[lecturer] At this time,

08:49.320 --> 08:52.740
I ask all students
to log into the Green Room for meditation.

08:52.823 --> 08:54.325
Countin’ on ya, Doc.

08:54.408 --> 08:56.285
[magical buzz]

08:56.369 --> 08:59.080
[static buzzing]

08:59.163 --> 09:00.581
-[man] Seriously?
-[girl] What?

09:00.665 --> 09:02.375
-[man] Martinez again!
-[indistinct chattering]

09:02.458 --> 09:05.836
-[indistinct chattering]
-[man] Not again!

09:05.920 --> 09:08.756
[grunting]

09:08.839 --> 09:11.926
[Gloria] I’m so sorry
for the inconvenience my son has caused.

09:12.009 --> 09:15.304
[principal] I wouldn't call this
a matter of money, Mrs. Martinez.

09:15.388 --> 09:19.433
Although I must say it was quite
an expense for us to restore the system.

09:19.517 --> 09:22.228
[Gloria] Of course,
and I will pay for the repairs.

09:22.311 --> 09:23.145
Hmm?

09:23.229 --> 09:26.857
As I understand it,
Mr. Martinez modified his headset

09:26.941 --> 09:30.903
with backalley software
to avoid paying for the licensed update.

09:30.987 --> 09:34.740
This is not behavior befitting a pupil
from a financially stable home.

09:34.824 --> 09:37.868
[Gloria] It's not a problem, really.
We can afford it.

09:37.952 --> 09:39.120
[principal] Be that as it may,

09:39.203 --> 09:41.956
I see an opportunity here
to improve David's situation.

09:42.039 --> 09:43.124
[Gloria] Meaning what, exactly?

09:43.207 --> 09:46.085
David is not a good fit
with his classmates.

09:46.168 --> 09:47.003
[groans]

09:47.086 --> 09:49.505
He could benefit
from a change in environment.

09:49.589 --> 09:52.717
No! Wait, please.
I mean, he has to stay here.

09:52.800 --> 09:56.262
He deserves this education as much
as every other child in this school.

09:56.345 --> 09:59.098
What happened?
Didn't I tell you to get the upgrade?

09:59.181 --> 10:02.310
Yeah. Doc's damn fault.
Gave me a faulty port drive.

10:02.393 --> 10:04.895
[Gloria] You tried to get around
the system, didn't you?

10:04.979 --> 10:07.315
Now, it'll cost us ten times more.

10:07.398 --> 10:08.733
[David] Sorry.

10:08.816 --> 10:10.359
[Gloria] If it's something
you gotta apologize for,

10:10.443 --> 10:12.445
maybe don't do it in the first place, hey?

10:12.528 --> 10:14.947
[David] You said you didn't have
the eddies when I asked, so…

10:15.031 --> 10:16.782
[Gloria] I was waiting for payday!

10:16.866 --> 10:19.952
You know we don't got that kind of cash
just lying around.

10:20.036 --> 10:22.997
Can't you sit still a minute? [sighs]

10:25.291 --> 10:28.044
[David] You know,
I've been thinkin’ lately.

10:28.127 --> 10:29.545
[Gloria] About what?

10:29.629 --> 10:33.174
[David] Maybe I drop out.
Find some work or whatever.

10:33.257 --> 10:34.842
[Gloria] Do you hear yourself?

10:34.925 --> 10:37.887
[David] C'mon, seriously.
You know we can't afford those repairs.

10:38.971 --> 10:43.684
Plus, you got no idea just how bad
I stand out compared to all of them.

10:43.768 --> 10:47.355
Anyone sides a true blue corpo
gets shit on.

10:47.438 --> 10:49.357
Even if I do graduate,
they'll never accept me.

10:49.440 --> 10:51.984
No kid from Santo will ever be a suit.

10:52.068 --> 10:53.986
I don't wanna be one anyway.

10:57.657 --> 10:58.783
So, you tell me.

10:58.866 --> 11:01.410
What have I been busting
my ass for then, huh?

11:02.078 --> 11:05.456
Everything I do, I do for you, D.

11:05.539 --> 11:06.832
Don't you see that?

11:06.916 --> 11:11.045
[sighs] You're breaking my heart, Miho.

11:11.128 --> 11:12.129
Wait. What?

11:12.213 --> 11:16.801
My sweet baby boy. So smart, so talented.

11:16.884 --> 11:18.135
You're everything to me.

11:18.219 --> 11:22.056
I want to give you a fighting chance
in this city and a good education.

11:22.139 --> 11:26.936
It's why I put in all of those hours.
Why I'm never home.

11:29.063 --> 11:30.606
[David] Uh, I'm sorry.

11:31.232 --> 11:35.027
Shouldn't have brought it up.
Don't cry, Mom.

11:35.111 --> 11:37.738
[Gloria] Think I don't know
how they treat you?

11:37.822 --> 11:39.740
Think I don't get treated the same way?

11:41.033 --> 11:43.577
But that's why you gotta prove them wrong.

11:43.661 --> 11:45.913
You have to work hard
and rise through the ranks.

11:45.996 --> 11:50.042
My son at Arasaka Tower top floor!
I can just see it.

11:50.126 --> 11:52.586
You've got this, D. You're my son.

11:53.170 --> 11:54.880
Yeah, well, easier said than done.

11:55.464 --> 11:57.383
-Huh?
-[Gloria shouts]

12:00.094 --> 12:02.847
-[David groans]
-[man 1] Fuck 'em up!

12:02.930 --> 12:05.307
-[David groans]
-[Gloria shrieks]

12:05.391 --> 12:08.644
-Don't let 'em get away!
-Suit's limo's titanium plated!

12:08.727 --> 12:11.188
[man 1] The hunt's on, my beastbros!

12:11.272 --> 12:12.606
-[man 1 laughing]
-[man 2 shouts]

12:23.033 --> 12:24.577
No one fucks with the Animals!

12:24.660 --> 12:27.204
-[man] Suckers…
-Mom! Brake! Brake hard!

12:27.288 --> 12:28.789
-[Gloria shrieks]
-Watch out!

12:34.378 --> 12:39.300
-[static buzzing]
-[David heaving]

12:40.092 --> 12:42.595
[stammers] Mom? Mom!

12:42.678 --> 12:46.265
-[fire blasting]
-[David breathing heavily]

12:46.348 --> 12:50.311
[tense music]

12:50.394 --> 12:53.397
Is that the Trauma Team? Oh, thank Christ.

12:55.274 --> 12:57.651
-[beeping]
-[man] He's not a client.

12:57.735 --> 12:59.195
[woman] Neither is she.

12:59.278 --> 13:00.237
Hey, wait!

13:00.321 --> 13:03.908
[man] Secure the policyholder.
Leave them to the city meat wagons.

13:03.991 --> 13:05.701
-[woman] Copy that.
-[David] What?

13:05.784 --> 13:08.454
What the hell? Hey! Where are you going?

13:09.413 --> 13:10.706
Shit!

13:10.789 --> 13:12.708
No way. Just gonna leave us here?

13:12.791 --> 13:15.711
Mom! Momma!

13:15.794 --> 13:17.713
Mom, wake up!

13:17.796 --> 13:19.715
Fucking piece of… [heaving]

13:19.798 --> 13:24.261
Mom! Dammit, get off me!

13:24.345 --> 13:27.973
Shit. Get the fuck off!
[indistint] Dammit!

13:28.057 --> 13:31.018
[groans] Mom!

13:31.101 --> 13:32.478
[shouts] Fuck!

13:36.440 --> 13:38.067
[doctor] Surgery was a success.

13:38.150 --> 13:41.195
Your mother hasn't come to just yet,
but she's stable.

13:41.278 --> 13:43.405
Need her to stay a few more nights.

13:43.489 --> 13:45.783
Oh. Then, is it okay if I see her?

13:45.866 --> 13:49.537
No can do, buddy.
Visitation ain't part of your package.

13:49.620 --> 13:51.038
Oh. Right.

13:51.121 --> 13:53.999
Anyway, I should get started
on the paperwork.

13:54.083 --> 13:55.501
Brought your mom's things.

13:55.584 --> 13:58.462
And don't forget to zip us those eds.
Got three days.

13:58.546 --> 14:00.047
-Uh…
-Yeah.

14:00.130 --> 14:01.465
[doctor] There's a reason everyone
in Night City

14:01.549 --> 14:03.133
-wants insurance.
-[sighs]

14:03.217 --> 14:04.218
Stay safe now.

14:04.969 --> 14:07.471
[David] Yeah, hoop ship. Version back.

14:08.264 --> 14:10.766
Is that all? You low-balling me? Huh?

14:11.559 --> 14:13.769
Nah, forget it, choom.

14:14.436 --> 14:16.355
Dammit! Hmm?

14:16.438 --> 14:18.857
["Who's Ready for Tomorrow" playing]

14:18.941 --> 14:20.609
What the fuck?

14:20.693 --> 14:22.027
-[rumbling]
-[heaving]

14:22.111 --> 14:23.737
♪ I ain't your average sicko ♪

14:23.821 --> 14:25.489
♪ I'm dead, just like disco ♪

14:25.573 --> 14:28.033
♪ My bank account
Is zero-zero-zero, oh no ♪

14:28.117 --> 14:29.994
Another account. Christ.

14:30.077 --> 14:33.539
Just enough. She saved so much.
Never knew.

14:34.248 --> 14:36.542
So, that, it settled the medical.

14:37.376 --> 14:38.669
[sighs]

14:38.752 --> 14:41.505
Still gotta cover rent. Huh?

14:42.131 --> 14:45.759
Doc? Hey, you get the still I sent?
Listen.

14:45.843 --> 14:50.014
Don't think I'd forgotten I owe you a kick
in the nuts for that shoddy bootleg.

14:50.097 --> 14:51.599
But check this.

14:52.224 --> 14:53.350
Cyberware.

14:53.976 --> 14:57.813
Yeah, looks, uh, military, doesn't it?

14:57.897 --> 14:59.523
How do you think it would fetch

14:59.607 --> 15:02.484
if I was interested
and the price was right?

15:03.277 --> 15:05.112
Not selling. Just want an estimate.

15:08.073 --> 15:10.910
Nah, fuck that noise.
No way it's that cheap.

15:13.913 --> 15:15.915
[sighs] Oh, come on, choom.

15:18.000 --> 15:20.044
Whatev! Wasn't selling anyways.

15:20.127 --> 15:23.881
By the way. Don't expect me
to push your XBDs at school anymore!

15:25.674 --> 15:28.427
Any pinchin' hack had taken me for a gonk.

15:29.511 --> 15:31.597
A Sandevistan.

15:31.680 --> 15:36.101
No serial number and what?
Military-grade, this thing, really?

15:36.185 --> 15:39.146
It definitely ain't legal. But whatev.

15:39.229 --> 15:41.649
Whoa! The hell are these specs?

15:44.693 --> 15:47.112
[upbeat music]

15:54.912 --> 15:56.580
Huh? Ah!

15:58.165 --> 16:01.126
-[all chuckling]
-[clicks tongue, scoffs]

16:02.002 --> 16:04.463
[man] Little piece of advice, Martinez.

16:04.546 --> 16:07.383
-Learn to take a hint.
-[David] About what?

16:07.466 --> 16:10.302
[man] Our class.
You're not welcome. Got it?

16:10.386 --> 16:11.929
[David] Huh? If this is about yesterday--

16:12.012 --> 16:14.223
-Who said anything about yesterday?
-[David] What?

16:14.306 --> 16:17.893
You probably figure I give you a hard time
'cause you're poor. Simply untrue.

16:17.977 --> 16:19.979
I'm rather charitably inclined.

16:20.062 --> 16:22.481
Not your fault you were born
on the wrong side of society.

16:22.564 --> 16:25.359
[inhales] There's no rule
that says a street kid

16:25.442 --> 16:26.860
-can't make it at the Academy,
-[sighs]

16:26.944 --> 16:28.612
provided they pay their way.

16:28.696 --> 16:31.448
What cracks my chrome
is something else entirely.

16:31.532 --> 16:32.866
-Know what?
-Look, choom.

16:32.950 --> 16:35.285
I haven't understood
a single thing coming out of your mouth.

16:35.369 --> 16:36.704
-That right there!
-Hmm…

16:36.787 --> 16:39.456
Time to get gone.
Just drop out, why don't ya?

16:39.540 --> 16:41.667
-Huh?
-You're a misfit, an anomaly.

16:41.750 --> 16:44.962
Human but trash, and there's nothing
that can change that.

16:45.045 --> 16:48.340
Rot in you runs as deep
as your bones, Martinez.

16:48.424 --> 16:51.844
Best you can do
is not spread it to the rest of us.

16:51.927 --> 16:53.470
Did I just short-circ?

16:53.554 --> 16:56.432
Said you didn't care
as long as I paid tuition.

16:56.515 --> 16:58.934
I heard your mommy came in
to see the principal,

16:59.018 --> 17:01.228
-[inhales]
-ask forgiveness for your little stunt.

17:01.311 --> 17:02.521
Caused quite a scene,

17:02.604 --> 17:05.566
crying for her baby boy,
begging for him not to get expelled.

17:05.649 --> 17:06.859
So shameless.

17:06.942 --> 17:09.653
You know, since we're chatting,
I've just always wondered.

17:09.737 --> 17:13.115
How could she afford to send you
to Arasaka Academy anyway?

17:13.198 --> 17:16.118
-[heavy breathing]
-Care to explain, Martinez?

17:16.702 --> 17:20.372
Go on. Tell us.
How does Mommy pay your way?

17:20.456 --> 17:22.750
What's any Night City bottomfeeder

17:22.833 --> 17:24.877
do to make a quick eurobuck, huh?

17:24.960 --> 17:28.505
Oh! A couple of pretty
salacious things come to mind.

17:28.589 --> 17:29.631
[David] Tired of this shit.

17:29.715 --> 17:32.634
-Hold on, choom. Who said we were done?
-Fuck off!

17:33.218 --> 17:34.303
[grunts]

17:35.345 --> 17:37.056
-[scoffs]
-[gasps]

17:37.139 --> 17:38.682
[grunting]

17:38.766 --> 17:40.559
-[groans]
-[chuckles]

17:41.935 --> 17:45.272
[mocking] Huh? Oh? What?

17:45.355 --> 17:48.609
Huh? Ha! [silly sounds]

17:48.692 --> 17:49.985
[groans]

17:51.320 --> 17:52.988
[straining]

17:53.072 --> 17:56.492
Got anything slotted?
Anime freeware maybe?

17:56.575 --> 18:01.497
-[straining]
-Hmm? Hmm. Aww!

18:02.915 --> 18:03.749
[groans]

18:04.374 --> 18:07.461
-[gasps]
-[silly fighting sounds]

18:11.215 --> 18:12.549
-[grunts]
-[fighting sounds]

18:14.802 --> 18:16.720
[grunting and groaning]

18:16.804 --> 18:19.681
[fighting sounds]

18:19.765 --> 18:21.642
[David shouts]

18:21.725 --> 18:23.060
[David] I knew it.

18:23.143 --> 18:28.023
Nothing like the Strongarms 400 to bring
out the best in your kung-fu chipware.

18:28.107 --> 18:30.400
Organic knuckles? Seriously?

18:30.484 --> 18:34.029
Wanna try me again?
I suggest you pack some serious chrome.

18:34.113 --> 18:35.948
-Or just drop out.
-[whimpering]

18:36.031 --> 18:38.534
You know what I'd prefer.

18:38.617 --> 18:43.872
-[somber music]
-[pained breathing]

18:43.956 --> 18:46.583
-[phone beeps]
-[doctor] Mr. Martinez?

18:47.417 --> 18:51.171
I'm calling in regards
to Gloria Martinez's condition.

18:51.839 --> 18:54.216
-Huh?
-She was stable this morning,

18:54.299 --> 18:57.678
but then her vitals began to nosedive
really out of nowhere.

18:57.761 --> 19:02.558
But you said the surgery was successful.

19:02.641 --> 19:05.978
True. But only so much
we can do on the discount package.

19:06.061 --> 19:09.148
Worn down as she was,
I doubt she'd had lasted much longer.

19:09.231 --> 19:11.191
-Overworked, seemed to me.
-[gasping]

19:11.275 --> 19:14.444
Anyway, I'm supposed to tell you
we offer some burial options.

19:14.528 --> 19:17.823
People in Night City
want corpo gigs for a reason, kid.

19:18.615 --> 19:21.827
[automated voice] Greetings, valued
customer. We are sorry for your loss.

19:21.910 --> 19:23.871
To ease things at this difficult time,

19:23.954 --> 19:26.039
we can deliver the body
of your dearly departed

19:26.123 --> 19:28.208
to your home or to a funeral home.

19:28.292 --> 19:29.459
Would you like to learn more?

19:29.543 --> 19:31.086
[David] I got a choice?

19:31.170 --> 19:33.755
Is our budget-friendly
cremation service right for you?

19:33.839 --> 19:37.926
Waive those pesky delivery fees
and bring your loved one home today.

19:38.010 --> 19:39.386
[man sobbing]

19:40.554 --> 19:43.932
-[machine buzzes]
-[melancholic music]

19:46.018 --> 19:47.144
[automated voice] Don't walk.

19:47.227 --> 19:48.896
-[principal] Good day, Mrs. Martinez.
-Don't walk.

19:48.979 --> 19:50.480
-We've received a quote for the repairs
-Don't walk.

19:50.564 --> 19:52.107
-to our system infrastructure.
-Don't walk.

19:52.191 --> 19:55.611
As agreed, I've sent you an e-mail
with the payment details.

19:55.694 --> 19:57.446
Also, perhaps you've had time to think?

19:57.529 --> 19:58.739
Do let me know.

19:58.822 --> 20:00.824
Just say the word
and we'll begin making arrangements

20:00.908 --> 20:03.285
for David's transfer
to another institution.

20:03.368 --> 20:05.704
[automated voice] Please note.
To maintain your utilities contract,

20:05.787 --> 20:08.457
you must pay a penalty of 500 euro-dollars

20:08.540 --> 20:12.336
in addition to any past
due amounts and late fees.

20:12.419 --> 20:14.338
If you cannot pay by the deadline,

20:14.421 --> 20:17.925
your services will be terminated
in the following order…

20:18.008 --> 20:20.677
[female voice] Trauma Team.
Clear a path immediately.

20:20.761 --> 20:22.804
-[female voice] …medical…
-[man] Ding-ding, Martinez!

20:22.888 --> 20:24.890
Me again. Time's up.

20:24.973 --> 20:27.184
Rent's long past due.

20:27.267 --> 20:29.853
Keep this shit up
and I won't just change your lock,

20:29.937 --> 20:32.940
I'll throw your ass out
on the street. You feel me?

20:33.023 --> 20:35.192
♪ City burn ♪

20:35.275 --> 20:40.364
♪ We're not planning to return ♪

20:40.447 --> 20:43.700
♪ Trying so hard to be free ♪

20:44.493 --> 20:49.206
-[rumbling]
-[straining]

20:49.289 --> 20:52.751
[David] The implant I showed you,
you said you'd take it off me for 10K?

20:53.835 --> 20:56.213
Six now? Said ten yesterday, choom!

20:56.296 --> 20:58.340
Come on. That's just one fucking day.

20:58.423 --> 21:00.592
And we both know that it's worth way more!

21:00.676 --> 21:02.844
Hell yeah, I looked into it, and I--

21:05.430 --> 21:08.517
Oh, yeah? Well, fuck you too! Bitch.

21:08.600 --> 21:10.018
[huffing]

21:14.314 --> 21:17.317
Katsuo here. I heard about your mom.

21:17.401 --> 21:21.071
I could offer my sympathies,
but find it hard to sympathize.

21:21.154 --> 21:23.240
God only knows what she had to endure

21:23.323 --> 21:26.243
to send her delinquent son to an Academy
he doesn't belong at.

21:26.994 --> 21:29.413
Her methods couldn't have been noble

21:29.496 --> 21:33.542
if she died in a car accident. So mundane.

21:33.625 --> 21:34.668
But you know?

21:34.751 --> 21:37.754
Karma. There's a lesson in this, David.

21:37.838 --> 21:39.006
[panicked breathing]

21:39.089 --> 21:41.925
Your mother tried to live
beyond her means and died.

21:42.676 --> 21:44.011
Don't make the same mistake.

21:44.094 --> 21:45.137
[panicked breathing]

21:53.228 --> 21:54.104
[erotic moaning]

21:54.187 --> 21:57.357
[man laughs wickedly]

21:57.441 --> 22:00.485
-[man gasps, grunts]
-[door buzzes]

22:00.569 --> 22:02.612
Christ. The hell. Who is that?

22:03.280 --> 22:05.615
-[chuckles] David, hey.
-[panting]

22:06.950 --> 22:08.744
That the big bad Sandy?

22:08.827 --> 22:12.331
Not a badge or fixer in town
who's not looking for that beauty.

22:12.414 --> 22:14.124
I told you though… [sniffs]

22:14.207 --> 22:18.045
ain't gonna find anyone
that's willing to take it off your hands.

22:18.128 --> 22:20.630
-[David] I'm not here to sell.
-[grunts]

22:20.714 --> 22:25.135
I want this fused here.
'Bout time I chrome the fuck up.

22:25.218 --> 22:28.638
[upbeat music]

22:34.519 --> 22:37.773
["This Fffire" playing]

22:44.321 --> 22:50.160
♪ Eyes, burning a way through me ♪

22:50.827 --> 22:56.333
♪ Eyes, destroying so sweetly ♪

22:57.250 --> 23:02.881
♪ Now, there's a fire in me ♪

23:02.964 --> 23:09.429
♪ A fire that burns ♪

23:36.998 --> 23:39.668
♪ This fire is out of control ♪

23:39.751 --> 23:43.547
♪ I'll burn it, I'll burn it ♪

23:53.014 --> 23:57.435
♪ I'll burn it, I'll burn it ♪
